  "wn41Sound": "A connection sound joins the vibration: the VPN hums a short note as it comes up or goes down (Settings → General).",
  "wn41RateUnit": "The speed reads in the unit you pick: the familiar KB/s or the connection's own Mbps.",
  "wn41BackgroundLock": "The app can lock itself while away: the password asks again right away, after 5, or after 15 minutes.",
  "wn41BiggerLimits": "The session's data limit climbs to 25, 50, or 100 GB.",
  "wn41Motion": "New motion: the connected orb breathes, the check draws itself in, the state's word glides between its values, and a wrong password shakes the field.",
  "wn41AboutFixed": "The About page sits straight: the two pages side by side, every hint on its own line, nothing squeezed.",
  "wn41HapticFixed": "The vibration setting answers again: every connection's on and off follows it, not just the slider's.",
  "copyIp": "Copy IP",
  "wn42Fonts": "Every language reads in the app's own faces: Noto Sans for the two Chinese and for Bengali, Inter for the Latin and Cyrillic ones — no language leans on the phone's fonts anymore.",
  "wn42Sounds": "The app's sounds are real now: a soft tap in every section, two notes for the switches, a rising and a falling note as the connection comes up and goes down, a ping for the lock — the sound switch gates them all.",
  "wn42AboutFixed": "The About page centers its logo, its name and its note, and the contact handles stay whole on one line whatever the phone's width.",
  "wn42Gaming": "The gaming profile is real now: the servers page measures the delays fresh every half minute and lifts the measured fastest with the accent.",
  "avatarPhoto": "Your photo",
  "avatarPhotoFailed": "That picture could not be used",
  "tlsFragmentAuto": "Auto",
  "tlsFragmentAutoHint": "The whole hello first; a network that keeps cutting TLS gets the name cut on its own, for half an hour",
  "accentDesign": "The design's own light",
  "wn45Designs": "Four new home looks — Aurora, Neon, Dusk and Sage — each dressing every page in its own palette",
  "wn45HelloAuto": "The TLS fragment learned: a network that keeps killing the handshake gets the name cut on its own, and the tunnel gets through",
  "wn45RelayRace": "Relay recovery now races three edges at once, so a filtered network finds its way back sooner",
  "wn45AccentFixed": "The accent picker lights the app again — its color had stopped reaching the pages",
  "wn45WhatsNewFixed": "The What's new page shows its words again — it had opened empty",
  "wn46Designs": "Two new looks from the reference designs: the aether's iOS status card and the zed's gradient blob — each dresses the whole app, every page, and the four earlier looks left.",
  "wn46Sounds": "The sounds grew a professional set: a swell for the connect that begins, a chord when it carries, a falling one when it rests, and a muted note for the blocked way — one voice at a time.",
  "wn47Designs": "The two reference looks now dress the whole app — every page, not just the home: the aether wears AetherST's iOS structure (the curved notch bar, the grouped tables, the colored badges, the system's own state colors), and the zed wears ZedSecure's expressive one (the floating dock, the very-round cards, the draggable tool bubbles).",
  "wn47Fixes": "A settings row that overflowed on narrow screens now reads to its end.",
  "wn48Bars": "The two designs' bottom bars hold their places again: the aether's blue circle rests in its own tab's notch, and the zed's circle no longer covers the name under it.",
  "wn48Fit": "The homes fit their screens again: the aether's card reads Disconnected to its end, the zed's orb steps down when the page runs tight, and while the connection is being made no track asks to slide to connect and no hint says disconnect at once.",
  "wn48Wheel": "The flags' wheel dissolves a card before the screen's edge can cut it, the recommended place wears Mozilla's mark at a size that reads, and the flat map's south edge melts into the page instead of ending in a line.",
  "wn49States": "The two reference designs wear the details they were drawn with: the aether's card carries the session's own rates the way AetherST's does, its power button breathes the reference's glow and sinks under the finger, and the zed's blob turns itself between its shapes while its center's selves cross-fade.",
  "wn49Words": "Connecting has a word everywhere now: while the tunnel is being made, the switch's track carries Connecting…, the knob's mark fades between its selves, and the track breathes with the connection's own rhythm — nothing vanishes under the finger.",
  "wn49Sooner": "The connection's engine is the original's own again: the relay pool, the alternate routes and their cache, and the repeated-request guard carry the tunnel — it comes up sooner and holds.",
  "wn49Mark": "The recommended location wears Mozilla VPN's real mark, and the update's buttons wear the update's own glyph.",
  "wn50Notch": "The two designs' dress comes out of the mess it had kept: the aether's notch bar reads the circle's own center, the chosen tab's name wears the page's ink on both looks, and the circle's glow keeps to the circle instead of washing the name.",
  "wn50Cards": "The zed's home folds its rates into the bento: the rate card joins the bento's two cells and the session's row, the page's last cards clear the dock's seat, and nothing runs half under the dock when the page scrolls to its end.",
  "wn50Veil": "The status band wears its veil: the scrolled content fades beneath the clock instead of colliding with it, the zed's pushed pages no longer start under the clock, and its floating tools keep clear of the dock's seat.",
  "wn50Ping": "The aether's ping chip measures again on a tap, the way the reference's own chip answers.",
  "tapToChangeServer": "Tap to change server",
  "wn51Smooth": "The flags' wheel and the strip move the way a wheel should: the drag and the change of country now ride the compositor — nothing re-lays out and no glow redraws itself while the flags turn, so the wheel spins smooth and the page scrolls with it.",
  "wn51Zed": "The zed's home wears the reference's own structure: the two rate cards stand under the brand (resting at their zeros when the tunnel rests), the state's word arrives in the display's big face under the orb, and the place lives on the bright server card above the dock — the small chip and the repeated name are gone.",
  "wn51Aether": "The aether's home says the place once: the strip's repeated name line rests, the status card and the power button keep their seats, and the page reads as one clean column.",
  "wn51Veil": "The clock's veil grew a breath tall and holds its color across the clock's band: the content that scrolls beneath it fades whole, and its words never meet the clock.",
  "wn52Speed": "The tunnel runs at the network's own speed again: the VPN's interface speaks the line's packet size (MTU 1500) instead of an oversized one, so downloads take their full speed and calls stay steady — on mobile data especially.",
  "wn52Smart": "Fastest location and the recommended service choose honestly again: every start measures the locations fresh and takes the best one now, instead of quietly riding the place chosen before.",
  "wn52Motion": "Thirty new animations, all over the app: every page and card lands softly, pressed tiles sink and return, the connecting state's dot breathes, and pushed pages glide in — each one standing still when the system asks for less motion.",
  "wn52Pages": "The pushed pages arrive with a soft glide and the page's title from its own edge; while a setting saves, a quiet line sweeps the section.",
  "wn56Button": "The connect slider keeps its word through the whole walk — no more empty moment between connecting and connected: the word glides between its states now, and the working dim follows with a breath.",
  "wn56Capsule": "The wheel's home says each state once: the repeated status word above the slider is gone — the track itself carries it, and the page reads a line quieter.",
  "wn56Door": "The speed test has its own door on the home: one row, one tap, and the measurement opens — before the first connect too, not only while the tunnel carries.",
  "wn56Wheel": "The flags' wheel glides: one fling carries one country, and the landing settles into place instead of snapping — the drag reads heavy and steady, the way a good dial turns.",
  "designGazette": "Gazette",
  "designGazetteDesc": "A front page: the masthead, the ruled columns and the ink stamp — the news sheet's own calm, in paper and ink",
  "designGta": "GTA",
  "designGtaDesc": "The game's own HUD: the weapon wheel that turns, the radar-green tunnel, the amber panels and the neon night",
  "speedTestSizesTitle": "Test size",
  "wn61Gta": "The GTA design: the game's own HUD — the weapon wheel for the flags, the radar-green tunnel, the amber panels, the heavy face and its own tick",
  "wn61Sound": "The wheel's tick: every seat the dial passes answers in the ear as well as the hand",
  "wn62Wheel": "The weapon wheel rebuilt: the seats keep the game's own spacing at any country count, the chosen sector carries the wheel's lit wedge, and a flick throws the dial",
  "wn62Map": "The home's map wears each design's own colors now — the water, the land and the grid follow the design the page carries",
  "wn62HudMap": "The GTA design's own map: the game's HUD plate — deep water, the neon coast, the amber radar grid and the sweep that walks the world while the tunnel carries",
  "wn62Aether": "The Aether design's power control rebuilt: the disc stands in a thin ring track, the connecting arc walks the ring, and the machined face catches the light",
  "wn62Gta": "The GTA connect pad answers the hand — the whole panel sinks on a press, and the power's mark steps back while the connection is being made",
